<title>USA: H.F. Ahmanson and Co Q4 net income rises.</title>
<headline>H.F. Ahmanson and Co Q4 net income rises.</headline>
<dateline>IRWINDALE, Calif. 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Call puts 1996 Q4 estimates at $0.60 a share.</p>
<p>				1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr diluted		$0.74		    $0.40</p>
<p> Net interest inc     317,722		  306,892</p>
<p> Net income		91,247		   60,709</p>
<p>		   12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.91		    $1.40</p>
<p> Net interest inc   1,252,514		1,226,755</p>
<p> Net interest inc     145,258		  216,204</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)  </p>
<p>NOTE: The 1996 fourth-quarter results include a gain on the sale of the company's San Antonio branches and other branch consolidation activities, as well as a refund of FDIC insurance assessments.</p>
<p>The 1996 full year results include an aftertax charge of $144.4 million related to a special assessment to recapitalize the Savings Association Insurance Fund (SAIF).</p>
<p>The 1995 full year results include an aftertax charge of $234.7 million related to an accounting change eliminating certain goodwill, and a $252.7 million aftertax gain in connection with sale of the retail branch system in New York.</p>
</text>
